{"4706030": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Spaceman's Luck", "steam_appid": 4706030, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "dlc": [4760590], "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A <strong>strategy/4X game where you take over space</strong>, made by hotshot game developer <strong>Gideon Kennedy </strong>of <strong>Gerrymap </strong>fame.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spaceman's Luck is like lightning crystallized into a video game. It shuns classic principles of the genre (being boring and sucking) and embraces <u><strong>4V: Vitality, Vigor, Virtue, and Virility</strong></u>. You <strong>colonize space</strong>, while trying to expand in the most Advantageous way. You go from star to star, and each one has planets. Some planets are Really Good, others Aren't. Some stars are Far, and others Close. Do I need to say more...?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4706030/extras/27411fae1ff9036ba922576529221d4d.poster.avif?t=1784405221\" width=540 height=124 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4706030/extras/27411fae1ff9036ba922576529221d4d.webm?t=1784405221\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4706030/extras/27411fae1ff9036ba922576529221d4d.mp4?t=1784405221\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is where the patented <strong>Luck</strong> mechanic comes in. A good Spaceman's <strong>Luck</strong> will allow you to win somewhat easily, and a bad Spaceman's <strong>Luck</strong> will kill you in real life. There are four default races representing the Tremendous Diversity of this wonderful Galaxy (and the <u><strong>4 V's</strong></u>): the Humans, Space Elves, Space Orcs, and Space Ants. Each has their own Strengths and Weaknesses.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Do you have a Spaceman's Luck?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A <strong>strategy/4X game where you take over space</strong>, made by hotshot game developer <strong>Gideon Kennedy </strong>of <strong>Gerrymap </strong>fame.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Spaceman's Luck is like lightning crystallized into a video game. It shuns classic principles of the genre (being boring and sucking) and embraces <u><strong>4V: Vitality, Vigor, Virtue, and Virility</strong></u>. You <strong>colonize space</strong>, while trying to expand in the most Advantageous way. You go from star to star, and each one has planets. Some planets are Really Good, others Aren't. Some stars are Far, and others Close. Do I need to say more...?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4706030/extras/27411fae1ff9036ba922576529221d4d.poster.avif?t=1784405221\" width=540 height=124 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4706030/extras/27411fae1ff9036ba922576529221d4d.webm?t=1784405221\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4706030/extras/27411fae1ff9036ba922576529221d4d.mp4?t=1784405221\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is where the patented <strong>Luck</strong> mechanic comes in. A good Spaceman's <strong>Luck</strong> will allow you to win somewhat easily, and a bad Spaceman's <strong>Luck</strong> will kill you in real life. There are four default races representing the Tremendous Diversity of this wonderful Galaxy (and the <u><strong>4 V's</strong></u>): the Humans, Space Elves, Space Orcs, and Space Ants. Each has their own Strengths and Weaknesses.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Do you have a Spaceman's Luck?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "short_description": "A space 4X game. Colonize planets and annihilate enemy races in an intergalactic war for living space. Designed to be fun, fast, and easy to play.", "supported_languages": "English", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4706030/b704aa1629f8411d33ff78de5d69d81966316eef/header.jpg?t=1784405221", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4706030/bb08840354d2928e01e018c5eb32d6480f0cb665/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1784405221", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4706030/bb08840354d2928e01e018c5eb32d6480f0cb665/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1784405221", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Core 2 Duo<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> GT 730</li></ul>"}, "mac_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> 11 (Big Sur)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Apple M1 or Intel Core M</li></ul>"}, "linux_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Arch Linux<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Core 2 Duo<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> GT 730<br></li><li><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> If you use a distri